+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+# fa3-metadata-fold-preattn-full-verify (log tag [fm]). On the three full-layer verify rows (window 0, q_len 8,
+# page 1, tp8; B = 1 unpaired at page-table width 80008, B = 16 / 32 paired at 86008: the judge's verify shapes at
+# ctx 80000, spread fixed at B = 1 and agentic at 16 / 32), FA3's varlen scheduler metadata (what its in-call
+# prepare_varlen_num_blocks_kernel<NumWarps, Sort=true> writes) is computed by ONE extra program of the existing
+# _pre_attention_kernel launch (META=True, grid (tokens + 1, Hq + Hkv)) from this call's cache_seqlens into a
+# per-call buffer and handed to flash_attn_with_kvcache as scheduler_metadata, so FA3 launches no prepare kernel.
+# Nothing derived from inputs is kept: only shape-only constants (block sizes, PackGQA, the static split cap, SM
+# count, the L2 block budget, the tie rule) are frozen per (B, page-table width). Gates per row: (a) recover those
+# constants by matching a Python port against the library's own get_scheduler_metadata (called as mha_fwd derives
+# it for kernel_fn's FA3 call) on judge draws plus edge sets, every surviving candidate must also match a 64-draw
+# holdout; (b) the Triton META program equals the library on every valid slot and the semaphore for every sample;
+# (c) kernel_fn's output, FA3's output and the whole k/v caches torch.equal to master's on 8 draws at the judge
